What are Welding Collaborative Robots?
Welding collaborative robots (cobots) represent a transformative evolution in industrial automation, combining the precision of robotic welding with the flexibility of human collaboration. These systems incorporate advanced safety features like force-limited actuators and real-time collision detection, enabling them to work safely alongside human operators without traditional safety cages.

Key variants include:

Arc welding cobots – Dominating metal joining applications
Spot welding cobots – Widely used in automotive assembly
Laser welding cobots – For high-precision applications

